# Frontend React

- Functional components only.
- All FastAPI calls live in a client module (e.g. `frontend/src/api.js`), not inside components.
- Core UI: file upload + toggles for definitions, diagrams, and code blocks (more filled vs more blank).
- Preview PDFs in container-sized panes. See `frontend-layout.mdc` for resize rules.
- Extract reusable hooks (e.g. `useContainerSize`) instead of inlining observers in components.
- Render the generated template simply. Print/export comes later.
- No homework chat, Q&A box, or "ask about this folder" UI.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — fetch + template logic inlined in the page
function App() {
  const onSubmit = async (e) => {
    const res = await fetch("/ingest", { method: "POST", body: new FormData(e.target) });
    setText(await res.json());
  };
}

// ✅ GOOD — component calls the API client
function UploadForm({ onIngested }) {
  const onSubmit = async (file, toggles) => {
    const source = await api.ingest(file);
    const template = await api.generateTemplate(source.id, toggles);
    onIngested(template);
  };
}
```
